A||N||6||87ECO5||Announcement from Paul McKibben||||14||
Z||000000||87ECO5||02-07-2001||06:20 AM||||Hey, guys and gals.  I was talking with Paul McKibben last night (via email) and he asked me to pass this on to the members of PFF:<P>.<P><I><BR>By the way, I just put up a new decal on my web site last night.  It's the "Pontiac" windshield decal.  It is a dead-on duplicate of the factory original. Unlike all the other aftermarket Pontiac windshield decals I've seen, this one is curved to match the top of the Fiero windshield and it doesn't get hit by the windshield wipers.  If any of your friends on Pennock's Forum are looking for one, let 'em know for me.<P>Thanks!<P>Paul<BR></I><P>.<P>I told him he needs to join the PFF ranks - at least long enough to add his name to the vendor list    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   - and become a part of the elite club!<P>Hopefully, we'll see Paul here soon.||||reg||14
Z||000001||Raydar||02-07-2001||09:35 AM||||For anyone who doesn't know...<BR>Paul McKibben is the Fiero Sail Panel guy.<BR>He does superb work. <P>Here's his site... <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||14
Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-07-2001||09:54 AM||||Paul has a great product and is an outstanding guy to deal with. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodney||02-07-2001||02:24 PM||||Fiero windshield and it doesn't get hit by the windshield wipers.<P>It would have to be less than 1" tall or you would have to have very short wiper blades for it not to get hit. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||02-07-2001||04:38 PM||||I think Paul McKibben is one hell of a nice guy. I picked up a set of custom panels from him last summer.<P>But......<BR>The paint on my panels keep bubbling off around the edges.... He has sent me 2 replacements, Its happening again on the drivers side. From what I understand no one else has had this problem. Is it possible to just make smoked plexi? (Not painted) I dont want to go with the 84 type. I feel like a dum**ss.. When I bought my car the panels were 100% MINT. When I changed them to the custom ones, I didnt know much about Fiero parts & how hard they were to find. I should have just used a whole new sail panel when I changed them....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Live & Learn<P><BR>My 2  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/penny_spin_md_clr.gif">  Paul is a good guy with great products...(Im just not having good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )<P>-Carl<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A>||||reg||10
Z||000005||Monkeyman||02-07-2001||06:03 PM||||DON'T SCARE ME LIKE THAT, SCOTT!!!!!!!!!<P>I thought you were going to tell us that Paul was going out of business.  Whew!  I haven't ordered my sail panels yet.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Black88GT||02-07-2001||06:16 PM||||Yeah Paul is definitely a good guy to deal with.  When I had my formula he sent me 3 different decals for one price to see which size looked best on the decklid.  Recently, I lent him my starter hole guide plate for a 3.4 and I had it back in my possesion within a week from the day I shipped it.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
